    {
      "gene": "CCND1",
      "resolved_as": "CCND1",
      "marked_druggable": false,
      "civic_best_level": "B",
      "civic_best_predictive_level": "B",
      "civic_pending_predictive_level": null,
      "civic_predictive": true,
      "civic_items": 5,
      "verdict": "REVIEWED",
      "note": "both level-B items are about tamoxifen rather than about hitting cyclin D1: CCND1 overexpression predicting RESISTANCE to tamoxifen (EID 856; PMID 15138475 says so in its title, and reports that the 46 strongly ER-positive, cyclin-D1-overexpressing tumours of 167 showed no survival difference between tamoxifen and no treatment) and CCND1 amplification failing to predict it in MA.12 (EID 858, DOES_NOT_SUPPORT; PMID 24367492, \"no statistically significant interaction with treatment was observed\", CCND1 copy number measured in 442 patients). The only item about a CDK4/6 inhibitor is level D, in cell lines (EID 1562; PMID 19874578, a panel of 47 breast cancer cell lines treated with palbociclib). The page keeps CCND1 as an unflagged oncogene, and the Targets lens already shows it under 'Reached only through a partner', via CDK4 and CDK6"
    },
    {
      "gene": "RB1",
      "resolved_as": "RB1",
      "marked_druggable": false,
      "civic_best_level": "B",
      "civic_best_predictive_level": "B",
      "civic_pending_predictive_level": null,
      "civic_predictive": true,
      "civic_items": 9,
      "verdict": "REVIEWED",
      "note": "both level-B items predict RESISTANCE -- RB1 phosphorylation with alpelisib (EID 1609; PMID 25002028, which calls the drug BYL719 and reports that responding tumours suppressed phospho-Rb while non-responders sustained it), and RB1 mutation among the alterations selected on palbociclib plus fulvestrant in PALOMA-3 (EID 12045; PMID 30206110, \"RB1 mutations emerged only in the palbociclib plus fulvestrant arm ... 6/127, 4.7%\") -- as does the level-C item, RB1 mutations emerging after CDK4/6 inhibition (EID 6097, SUBMITTED; PMID 29236940, three patients). That is what the page already says: the CDK4 target card calls RB1 a negative biomarker rather than a target, and the Targets lens lists it under 'Altered often, nothing against it'"
    },
    {
      "gene": "TP53",
      "resolved_as": "TP53",
      "marked_druggable": false,
      "civic_best_level": "B",
      "civic_best_predictive_level": "B",
      "civic_pending_predictive_level": null,
      "civic_predictive": true,
      "civic_items": 19,
      "verdict": "REVIEWED",
      "note": "each of the three level-B items selects an older drug on TP53 status, and two of the three are the paper's own: DNA-binding-domain (EID 2783) and L3-domain (EID 3036, SUBMITTED) mutations predicting RESISTANCE to tamoxifen, PMID 10786679 reporting that tumours mutated in codons that directly contact DNA, or in the zinc-binding L3 loop, had the lowest response to tamoxifen (18% and 15%, against 66% for wild type). The third, R249 predicting response to doxorubicin, is **the item's and not the paper's** (EID 399, \"more responsive to doxorubicin than breast tumors with wild type TP53\"): PMID 9569050 names no therapy in its abstract, which reports relapse-free and overall survival only, and Europe PMC's PMC2150115 record is flagged is-scanned, its body served as page images with no text layer, so the 9,641 characters it returns are front matter and that same abstract -- 0 hits for doxorubicin, chemotherap or tamoxifen. The article body cannot be read at all. Attribute it to EID 399 (INV-19). None of the three is a drug aimed at TP53, which is what the glossary line and the 'Altered often, nothing against it' list say"
    },
